Subject: ws2_32: IPv4-only getaddrinfo by default, WINE_DISABLE_IPV6=0 opts out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On a network with no working IPv6 (common behind a proxy/VPN), Steam resolves
its Connection Manager / directory hosts (api.steampowered.com, *.steamserver.net)
to IPv6 addresses, connects to them, and hangs at login on
STATUS_HOST_UNREACHABLE (0xc000023d) — the client never reaches a CM and the
login window never appears.

Pin getaddrinfo()'s ai_family to AF_INET so only A records are returned and
steamclient uses the working IPv4 path. Confirmed with WINEDEBUG=+winsock:
api.steampowered.com flips from AF_INET6 to AF_INET 184.31.138.105.

This is the default rather than an opt-in. It was WINE_DISABLE_IPV6=1 set by the
launcher on every bottle, which made it a constant that every harness standing
in for a GUI launch had to mirror by hand, and those mirrors drift.
WINE_DISABLE_IPV6=0 restores upstream resolution, per bottle or per program.

Only applied when the caller expressed no preference (ai_family == AF_UNSPEC).
An app that asks for AF_INET6 has said something specific, and handing it A
records would be a wrong answer rather than a narrowed one — addresses it cannot
use, or EAI_* for an IPv6 literal, with nothing explaining why.

diff --git a/dlls/ws2_32/unixlib.c b/dlls/ws2_32/unixlib.c
index e0e1263e025..4b71d560e54 100644
--- a/dlls/ws2_32/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/ws2_32/unixlib.c
@@ -704,7 +704,7 @@ static NTSTATUS unix_getaddrinfo( void *args )
     struct addrinfo *unix_info, *src;
     struct WS_addrinfo *dst, *prev = NULL;
     unsigned int needed_size = 0;
-    int ret;
+    int ret, force_v4 = 0;
 
     /* servname tweak required by OSX and BSD kernels */
     if (service && !service[0]) service = "0";
@@ -751,7 +751,27 @@ static NTSTATUS unix_getaddrinfo( void *args )
         }
     }
 
-    ret = getaddrinfo( params->node, service, hints ? &unix_hints : NULL, &unix_info );
+    /* IPv4-only resolution unless WINE_DISABLE_IPV6=0. On a network with no
+     * working IPv6, Steam resolves its CM/directory hosts (api.steampowered.com,
+     * *.steamserver.net) to dead IPv6 addresses, connects, and hangs at login
+     * (STATUS_HOST_UNREACHABLE 0xc000023d). Pinning ai_family to AF_INET makes
+     * getaddrinfo return only A records, so steamclient takes the IPv4 path.
+     *
+     * Only when the caller expressed no preference. An app that asks for
+     * AF_INET6 has said something specific, and answering with A records would
+     * be a wrong answer rather than a narrowed one -- it would get addresses it
+     * cannot use, or EAI_* for an IPv6 literal, with no way to tell why. This is
+     * a default for the ambiguous case, not an override of an explicit one. */
+    {
+        const char *no_v6 = getenv( "WINE_DISABLE_IPV6" );
+        if ((!no_v6 || no_v6[0] != '0') && unix_hints.ai_family == AF_UNSPEC)
+        {
+            unix_hints.ai_family = AF_INET;
+            force_v4 = 1;
+        }
+    }
+
+    ret = getaddrinfo( params->node, service, (hints || force_v4) ? &unix_hints : NULL, &unix_info );
     if (ret)
         return addrinfo_err_from_unix( ret );
 
